 36K  c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2021Ko08:                          
 36K 2c  Nature Physics 17, 439 (2021)                                          
 36K  c  Compiled by E.A. McCutchan (NNDC,BNL), July 6,  2021                   
 36K  c  1 GeV proton beam incident on a UC{-x} target followed by surface      
 36K 2c  ionization and mass separation using a high-resolution separator (HRS).
 36K 3c  Ions then cooled and bunched in a linear Paul trap (ISCOOL). Laser     
 36K 4c  spectroscopy performed with the Collinear Resonance Ionization         
 36K 5c  Spectroscopy (CRIS) setup at the ISOLDE facility at CERN.  Measured    
 36K 6c  energy differences between atomic hyperfine transitions; deduced       
 36K 7c  isotope shift and charge radius.                                       
